      correctIndex: 0,
      explanation: `<div style="border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; overflow:hidden"><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:8px 8px 0 0; color:white; padding:20px"><h1 style="color:white; margin:0">Available-for-Sale Securities: Unrealized Losses</h1></div><div style="background-color:white; padding:20px"><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Correct Answer</h3><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> <span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">A reduction in the carrying amount of the investment and an unrealized loss of $20,000 recognized in other comprehensive income.</span></p></div><div style="background-color:#f0f7fa; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Explanation</h3><p style="margin:0">When a company classifies investments as available-for-sale (AFS), changes in fair value between reporting periods result in unrealized gains or losses. According to accounting standards (FASB ASC 320), these unrealized gains or losses for AFS securities should be:</p><ul style="margin:0 0 12px 0; padding-left:22px"><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Excluded from net income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Reported as a component of other comprehensive income (OCI)</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Accumulated in a separate component of shareholders&#x27; equity</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Analysis of InvestMate&#x27;s Investment</li></ul><table cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:15px; width:100%"><thead><tr><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Event</th><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Initial investment (March 1, Year 1)</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$300,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Fair value (December 31, Year 1)</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$280,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Unrealized loss</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$20,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p style="margin:0">Since the bonds are classified as available-for-sale, the $20,000 decrease in fair value represents an unrealized loss. This unrealized loss does not affect net income but must be recognized in other comprehensive income and will result in a reduction of the carrying amount of the investment.</p></div><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:0 0 8px 8px; color:white; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:white; margin:0 0 12px 0">Summary</h3><ul style="margin:0 0 12px 0; padding-left:22px"><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">For available-for-sale securities, changes in fair value between reporting periods:</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Adjust the carrying amount of the investment on the balance sheet</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Create unrealized gains or losses that are reported in other comprehensive income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Do not affect net income unless the securities are sold or determined to be other-than-temporarily impaired</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Are tracked in the equity section as &quot;Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income&quot;</li></ul></div></div></div>`,
